meta {
  name: Get Course Eligibility Criteria
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/colleges/by-slug/{{collegeSlug}}/courses/{{courseId}}/eligibility-criteria?student_type=indian&quota_category=quota_general
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  student_type: indian
  quota_category: quota_general
}

docs {
  Dedicated endpoint for course eligibility criteria — NOT the same as the
  generic GET .../courses/:courseId/tabs/eligibility_criteria endpoint.
  That generic route returns the raw stored JSON verbatim (no resolution).
  This endpoint resolves the actual criteria list for a student type
  (and, for Indian students, a quota).

  Indian students choose a quota and each quota has its own criteria.
  Foreign students have no quota concept — they get one shared criteria
  list.

  Path params:
  - collegeSlug: College subdomain slug
  - courseId: Course ID

  Query params (both optional):
  - student_type: indian | foreign — no default; omitted/invalid means "no
    selection yet"
  - quota_category: a quota `id` from the `quotas` array below — only
    relevant when student_type=indian; ignored for "foreign"

  `criteria` is ONLY resolved once a real selection is made:
  - student_type=foreign → criteria is the shared foreign_student list
  - student_type=indian AND quota_category=<a real quota id> → criteria is
    that quota's list
  - student_type=indian with no/invalid quota_category → criteria is `[]`
    (a quota hasn't been picked yet)
  - no student_type at all → criteria is `[]` (nothing selected yet) —
    `student_types` and `quotas` are still returned so the client can render
    the filter UI before anything is picked

  Response:
  {
    "student_types": [
      { "value": "indian", "label": "Indian Student" },
      { "value": "foreign", "label": "Foreign Student" }
    ],
    "quotas": [{ "id", "label" }],
    "criteria": [{ "heading", "description" }],
    "filters_applied": { "student_type", "quota_category" }
  }

  `quotas` always lists the Indian-student quotas (for building a quota
  dropdown), regardless of the current student_type/criteria resolution.
  `filters_applied` echoes back exactly what was resolved (both null when
  nothing was selected or selection didn't match anything real).
  All text fields (`label`, `heading`, `description`, quota `id`) are
  trimmed of leading/trailing whitespace.

  Response message: "Eligibility criteria fetched successfully" (distinct
  from the generic tabs endpoint's "College section fetched successfully").
  Returns 404 "Course not found" if the course/college doesn't exist or
  isn't active.

  Table: courses (eligibility_criteria JSONB column)
}
